Card and BNPL screens now show this month's and next month's dues as two swipeable cards, each with its own total, paid, and left to pay — and you can pay next month early.
BNPL purchases are now real dues: every purchase gets its own due date, appears under next due and overdue, and can be paid on its own or together with the rest of that day's bill. Payment history shows exactly which purchases and installments a payment settled.
